WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
A bus needs a route through a changing city.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:16.000
A digital twin uses observations to explore the options.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:24.000
The route is ready before the junction.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:32.000
But the answer relies on an older picture of the road.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:40.000
The answer arrived on time. The world had changed.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:48.000
What if we update every digital state immediately?

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:56.000
At scale, those updates compete for limited bandwidth.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:04.000
Sending everything can leave important changes waiting.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:12.000
Which update matters most to this decision?

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:20.000
The oldest information is not always the most relevant.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:28.000
Freshness must be considered together with the task.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:36.000
Fresh information still needs computation.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:44.000
The nearby edge may be busy. The cloud needs communication.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:52.000
Faster processing can also compete with an energy budget.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:02:00.000
Time-critical scheduling is central to my research.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:08.000
Yet scheduling problems come with diverse objectives and constraints.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:16.000
A method that fits one problem may not fit the next.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:24.000
We study these problems through modeling and theoretical optimization.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:32.000
We develop and evaluate methods for execution and state updates.

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:40.000
We also explore AI-assisted algorithm design across diverse problems.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:48.000
Candidates must satisfy constraints and be evaluated.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:56.000
This complements our research on scheduling and optimization.

00:02:56.000 --> 00:03:04.000
We will also investigate adaptive scheduling under changing conditions.

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:12.000
The goal is timely, relevant information for a changing world.